      "writtenOn": "2024-04-17T16:49:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s true, if we were to create a YUVA image from existing TextureProxyViews, this would be clunky. At the moment, no one creates an image that way, there\u0027s always some transform applied to their source array.\n\nWe could instead have a factory that took a span of texture proxy views, and handled all the validation. It would iterate and check for null proxies, and the callers would just fill out an array and could choose to either early out if there was a null plane conversion or be optimistic and let the main factory just fail if a plane actually failed.\n\nThat also has the benefit of avoiding creating a `std::function` that has to capture local state, and syntax-wise a for-loop over the planes is pretty trivial to repeat at the call sites. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "3ce05054_f5b82534",
